# The game's own content. NEVER commit this.
#
# The code in this repository is free software and may be shared. Arx Fatalis'
# art, sound, levels and speech are Arkane Studios' and may not. Players must
# use their own copy of the game. Committing any of it here is the one mistake
# that could get this repository taken down - and because git keeps history,
# deleting it afterwards would not undo it.
# Anchored with a leading slash so they mean THESE folders, at the top of the
# repository, and nothing else. Unanchored, "game/" matches a directory called
# game at any depth - which quietly swallowed src/game/, the engine's own source.
# Its files were already tracked so they still committed, but git refused to
# stage them by name, and a NEW file added there would never have been committed
# at all, with nothing to say so.
/game/
/data/
*.pak
*.ftl
*.tea
*.dlf
*.fts
*.llf

# Build output
build/
*.exe
*.dll
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lib

# Local snapshots and older working copies - large, and history covers it now
backups/
best/
best-2/
best-3/
best-4/
*.rar
*.zip
*.7z

# Working files that mean nothing on anyone else's machine
*.log
arx.log
cfg.ini
*.sav
coop-profile-*.bin
coop-transfer.sav

# The screenshots live in docs/screenshots; this is the folder they came from
git hub pic/

# Editors and operating systems
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Packaged releases - these go on the GitHub releases page, not in the repo
release/

# A working copy of the engine's sources, kept beside the mod for reference.
# It was hidden by the unanchored "game/" rule above; now that that is anchored,
# it needs saying outright - it is 500 KB of somebody else's tree and does not
# belong in this repository's history.
/coop-source/engine-files/

# Locally unpacked game scripts and pages generated from them. The data is
# Arkane's and must never be committed.
/unpak-scripts/
/Script Map.html
/Engine Map.html
# A disposable local sandbox copy of the game - never ours to commit.
/game-studio/
# Locally exported level data - derived from the game's own files, so it
# must never reach the public repository.
/exports/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
